 "drivingQuestion": "If he transgressed and accepted it, may he leave it for the next winepress?",
 "outcome": "inconclusive",
 "outcomeNote": "the cited mishna and its testing follow in the next unit",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "chagigah.25a.12",
   "daf": "25a",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "עָבְרוּ הַגִּיתּוֹת וְהַבַּדִּים וְהֵבִיאוּ לוֹ חָבִית שֶׁל יַיִן — לֹא יְקַבְּלֶנָּה הֵימֶנּוּ, אֲבָל מַנִּיחָהּ לַגַּת הַבָּאָה. בְּעוֹ מִינֵּיהּ מֵרַב שֵׁשֶׁת: עָבַר וְקִיבְּלָהּ, מַהוּ שֶׁיַּנִּיחֶנָּה לַגַּת הַבָּאָה? אֲמַר לְהוּ: תְּנֵיתוּהָ:",
   "en": "§ It was taught in the mishna: Once «the» periods of the «winepress and olive press have passed,» if amei ha’aretz «brought to» a ḥaver priest a «barrel of teruma wine, he may not accept it from them. But» the giver «may leave it» over «for the following winepress» season, in the following year. «They raised a dilemma before Rav Sheshet:» If the priest «violated» the halakha «and did accept» the wine from an am ha’aretz, «what is» the halakha? Is it permissible «that he should leave it» over for himself «for the following winepress» season? Since it is permissible to accept the wine and oil of an am ha’aretz intentionally left until that time, perhaps it is also permissible if the priest himself intentionally leaves it over until that time. «He said to him: You learned it» in a mishna (Demai 6:9):"
  }
 ],
